# Copy to .env.local and replace the placeholder before starting the local stack.
# This file is intentionally safe to commit; .env.local is ignored.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-long-random-local-password
TRACERA_AUTH_TOKEN=replace-with-a-long-random-token
# Only set this when opting into the legacy split frontend stack:
# TRACERA_LEGACY_LOCAL_STACK=1
# TRACERA_LOCAL_PORT=18081

# --- Legacy bridge (off unless LEGACY_BASE_URL is set) -------------------
# Base URL of the legacy service that receives requests for 501-stub routes
# and for any LEGACY_OWNED_PREFIXES paths.
# LEGACY_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# Comma-separated path prefixes always owned by the legacy service. Matched on
# path-segment boundaries only ("/legacy" owns "/legacy/x" but not "/legacyx").
# LEGACY_OWNED_PREFIXES=/legacy,/old-api
# The bridge relays the caller's `authorization` header verbatim and runs after
# require_bearer, so the legacy service MUST accept the same bearer token as
# this server (TRACERA_AUTH_TOKEN) or it will answer 401/403, which is relayed
# as-is. Upgrade/websocket and SSE requests on owned prefixes are rejected with
# 501; the legacy service must not rely on them through this bridge.
# NOTE: method/stub disagreement (a method served by Rust on a path template
# that is otherwise a stub) is not yet detected at startup; audit routes by
# comparing router.rs registrations against the legacy surface before enabling.
